        Root cause:
        The `smk_cipso_doi()` function did not properly delete the old CIPSO DOI definition and its default mapping before attempting to re-add a previously used DOI value. When a DOI value that had been used earlier was written again, the old DOI entry still existed in the CIPSO subsystem, causing `netlbl_cfg_cipsov4_add()` to fail with error -17 (EEXIST). Since the old default map had already been removed before the new DOI attempt, the system ended up with no IPv4 default mapping, disabling networking for non-ambient labels. Additionally, concurrent writes to `/smack/doi` were not serialized, potentially causing inconsistent states.

